Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:09:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 067/106] Bluetooth: hci_qca: declarar HFP hw offload en el
 wcn3990

Sin QCA_CAP_HFP_HW_OFFLOAD el nucleo nunca anuncia data path 1 y el chip
mantiene dormidos sus puertos de audio SLIMBus (NACKea todo acceso).
Verificado: con el offload y un SCO con data path 1, los accesos que
antes fallaban completan.
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
index cd1834246..bd4981463 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2142,6 +2142,16 @@ static const struct qca_device_data qca_soc_data_wcn3990 __maybe_unused = {
 		{ "vddch0", 450000 },
 	},
 	.num_vregs = 4,
+	/*
+	 * The WCN3990 can carry HFP/SCO audio over its non-HCI (SLIMBus) path
+	 * instead of tunnelling it through HCI. Advertising the offload makes
+	 * the core hand data path id 1 to the controller in
+	 * HCI_Enhanced_Setup_Synchronous_Connection, which is what tells the
+	 * chip to bring its SLIMBus audio ports up - without it those ports
+	 * stay asleep and NACK every register access. Same capability the
+	 * wcn6855/wcn7850/qca2066 already declare.
+	 */
+	.capabilities = QCA_CAP_HFP_HW_OFFLOAD,
 };
 
 static const struct qca_device_data qca_soc_data_wcn3991 __maybe_unused = {
